cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "HPC Dashboard: seeing what an HPC job actually used"
abstract: >-
  A desktop application that reads job telemetry from shared HPC storage over
  SFTP and presents per-core utilisation, memory, I/O and GPU behaviour, plus
  recommendations for future resource requests based on the scheduler's real
  charging model. Reads files only; nothing runs on the cluster on the user's
  behalf.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sam
    family-names: Green
    affiliation: "ARC Centre of Excellence for 21st Century Weather, UNSW Sydney"
repository-code: "https://github.com/greensh16/hpc_dashboard_public"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.4
keywords:
  - high-performance computing
  - job monitoring
  - resource efficiency
  - Tauri
  - research software
